# Packages the running system needs that install/omarchy-base.packages does not
# name, because on x86_64 the ISO installs them from install/omarchy-other.packages.
#
# Format: <package name> <reason>
#
# That file is the ISO builder's cache list, not an install list, so most of it
# is firmware and drivers a running install has no business pulling. These are
# the ones whose absence is visible on a finished machine, each one measured on
# the aarch64 VM rather than assumed. Every entry has to exist in
# omarchy-other.packages: this file makes an ISO-only package reachable, it does
# not invent new dependencies.

# Omarchy ships /usr/lib/systemd/zram-generator.conf.d/90-omarchy.conf and a
# migration that moves older tuning into it. Without the package that config
# configures nothing and the machine has no compressed swap at all.
zram-generator  the shipped zram tuning has nothing to act on without it

# PipeWire itself comes in as a dependency of wireplumber, but its PulseAudio
# server does not. Without it `pactl info` answers "Connection refused", three
# shipped omarchy-audio-* commands talk to nothing, the shipped
# omarchy-speaker-tuning.service has no server to tune, and every application
# that speaks the PulseAudio API rather than PipeWire's own is silent.
pipewire-pulse  the PulseAudio compatibility server, which pactl and most apps need
